# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""/procedimientos/levantamiento-y-aumento-de-senos — Spanish copy.

The page's own statement is the reason it exists, and it argues against the
operation it is selling:

  "Hacer las dos a la vez es un compromiso real."
  A lift tightens the skin envelope; an implant pushes outward against it. They
  work against each other, which is why some surgeons stage them and why one
  sitting carries a higher revision rate than either alone. The page tells the
  reader to ask him which he recommends rather than assume one operation is
  simply more efficient. Nobody sells against their own combined procedure —
  keep it.

Same Evidence discipline as /levantamiento-de-senos: his before-and-afters for
this are filed under breast augmentation and are not shown here as though they
were this operation, and no timeline is invented for it.
"""

